            <ArticleTitle>Tacrolimus-induced pain syndrome in a pediatric orthotopic liver transplant patient.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>435-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Post-transplant complications are common among patients receiving immunosuppressive medications, including pain syndromes. Recently, a pain syndrome, calcineurin-inhibitor induced pain syndrome (CIPS) has been described. To our knowledge, this article is the second report of tacrolimus-associated CIPS, and the first report in the pediatric setting.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
